WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:01.310
Speaker 1: All right.

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:07.569
Last week, I interviewed Vincent Racaniello,
virologist from Columbia University, and he

00:00:07.569 --> 00:00:14.040
said it does make some sense that countries
are starting to roll back COVID guidelines

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.920
and restrictions.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:20.650
When you look at the U.K., when you look at
Israel, when you look at other countries,

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:26.490
it makes some sense because as this Omicron
wave goes down, it does seem like Macron is

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.480
significantly less deadly.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.759
Doesn't mean everybody has only a cold.

00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:35.970
But there are some reports that say the R
Macron death rate is 0.2 percent.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:41.050
That would put it at basically flu, which
is zero point one five percent.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:46.570
Vaccines widely available very good at preventing
serious illness and death are Macron tailored

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:52.660
vaccine coming in a few months, if not after
this wave than when is sort of the question

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.530
that is increasingly being asked.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:58.310
Of course, bearing in mind, some people are
going to need to be careful for a long time

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:01.030
because of specific health situations.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:04.710
Denmark is now going back to normal.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:09.960
Denmark will end most COVID restrictions and
quote Welcome the life we knew before.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:17.549
Denmark Prime Minister Medha Frederiksen announced
yesterday that Denmark will throw out most

00:01:17.549 --> 00:01:22.069
COVID pandemic restrictions that it placed,
including masks.

00:01:22.069 --> 00:01:25.659
Restrictions currently in place are for the
public to wear masks on public transit in

00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:29.619
restaurants, shops, health care facilities
and retirement homes.

00:01:29.619 --> 00:01:35.110
However, following the Feb. one change of
restrictions, which is Tuesday, masks will

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:39.210
only be required in hospitals, health care
facilities and elderly homes.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:43.680
We say goodbye to the restrictions and welcome
the life we knew before, Frederiksen said.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:50.950
As of February 1st, Denmark will be open,
according to Health Minister Magnus Handke.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:55.090
Denmark's recent cases of COVID were more
than 46000 daily on average.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:59.979
However, only 40 people are in hospital intensive
care units.

00:01:59.979 --> 00:02:05.490
We continue with a strong epidemic surveillance,
then we can react quickly if necessary.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:10.750
Despite lift of restrictions, Frederiksen
warned there could be a rise in infections,

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:15.270
which may lead to a fourth vaccination shot
being necessary, which other countries have

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:18.330
found doesn't actually make sense.

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:23.909
So there are certainly controversies here,
but this is a question many countries are

00:02:23.909 --> 00:02:24.970
going to be faced with.

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:27.770
I don't pretend to know the answer.

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:34.540
One aspect of this that many doctors are pointing
to is if not after this wave, than when.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:39.730
Because if this wave moves us to the endemic
phase where it takes on more of a flu like

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:47.200
seasonal trajectory with a lower death rate,
this secondary R Macron variant that now is

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:51.129
being looked at, which may be even more contagious
but even mild there, although we don't yet

00:02:51.129 --> 00:02:56.540
know for sure, would push us even closer to
flu slash cold.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:57.560
What do you wait for?

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:02.370
Is the question, and it's not for me about
are we now at no risk?

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:08.480
It's what milestone would we we be waiting
for if indeed, that's the trajectory, so I'm

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:15.819
not pretending to know what needs to happen,
but I am asking what would be the milestones

00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:22.819
if not in another six weeks as the cases continue
to decline rapidly, if they do.

00:03:22.819 --> 00:03:27.110
In many states, Massachusetts, for example,
cases are already down more than 50 percent

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:28.849
and declining very rapidly.

00:03:28.849 --> 00:03:32.380
Nationally, they're declining a little less
quickly.

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:35.390
Globally, they're basically flat right now.

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:38.299
Globally, we're now at the peak rather than
beyond it.

00:03:38.299 --> 00:03:44.189
So more and more countries going in this direction
doesn't seem the U.S. is close to it.

00:03:44.189 --> 00:03:49.250
I think masks on planes and public transit
will be around for a while, but there may

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.500
be changes coming.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:54.739
I'm curious to hear from you what direction
you think it needs to go.

